## Current phase

Phase 1 = **technical foundation** (complete for Cloud Backend / Local Admin shell).  
iOS: Phase 1 complete; Phase 1.5 Navigation Skeleton & Screen Shells only (Notion).  

**Backend/Admin V2** (operational expansion) is required and tracked under GitHub [#49](https://github.com/natefox2017/cookapp/issues/49) — AI Platform, AI Import, Analytics/Payments, Audit, Media abstraction.  
Do **not** treat mock Admin pages or missing Admin APIs as production-complete.  
Contract matrix: `docs/backend/ADMIN_API_CONTRACT.md`.

Forbidden without a matching Issue under #49 / product confirmation: inventing business AI features, fake production KPIs, Google Play “live” mock revenue.

## Locked stack

- iOS: Swift 6, SwiftUI, Swift Concurrency, Observation, MVVM, Feature Modules, DI, Protocol-oriented
- UI: Apple iOS 26 Liquid Glass + HIG; native SwiftUI first
- Backend: Supabase (Auth, DB, Storage, Functions)
- Auth: Sign in with Apple + Google → Supabase Auth (never store third-party tokens)
- Pay: StoreKit 2 + RevenueCat (decoupled from business)
- Bundle ID (Phase 1): `com.natefox.cookapp`

## Owner config (non-blocking)

Human dashboard secrets live in `docs/OWNER_CONFIG.md`.  
**Missing config must not block development** — use placeholders and continue other work.

## Workflow

Notion → GitHub Issue → Branch → Implement → Test → PR → Review → Merge  
Every code change must link an Issue. Prefer open-source integration over reinventing.
Agent merges ready PRs when checks pass (do not wait for user to click merge).
